  "blurb": "The far end of the Near Trapps cliff in the Shawangunks, a short stroll along the base trail beyond the Gelsa area. This is the Gunks' hard-climbing wall: half of its twenty trad lines are 5.12, with a good number of 5.10 and 5.11 routes and a few easier ones to warm up on, so it rewards fit leaders who place gear quickly. A few lines are also set up as top-ropes. Expect quartz conglomerate with the horizontal breaks and roofs the Gunks are known for."
